---
import StarlightPage from '@astrojs/starlight/components/StarlightPage.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../components/CodeBlock.astro';
import Explainers from '../components/Explainers.astro';
import Hero from '../components/home/Hero.astro';
import Install from '../components/Install.astro';
import BrunelRaster from '../components/live/BrunelRaster.astro';
import LifScope from '../components/live/LifScope.astro';
import SurrogatePlot from '../components/live/SurrogatePlot.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import { checks, results } from '../data/checks.mjs';
import { colab, repository, source } from '../data/site.mjs';
import model from '../../public/pilot/pilot.json';
import brunel from '../../snippets/brunel.py?raw';
import neuron from '../../snippets/neuron.py?raw';
import pilot from '../../snippets/pilot.py?raw';
import train from '../../snippets/train.py?raw';
import '../styles/page.css';

const evaluation = model.evaluation as Record<string, number>;
const trained = (model.meta as { trained: { steps: number; batch: number; horizon: number } }).trained;
const percent = (x: number) => `${Math.round(x * 1000) / 10}%`;
const kinds = { exact: 'Same numbers', tolerance: 'Within a tolerance', statistics: 'Same statistics' };
---

<StarlightPage
	frontmatter={{
		title: 'sparx: spiking neural networks in JAX',
		description: 'Train spiking networks with gradients or local rules, and simulate circuits of biological neurons in millivolts and milliseconds, in JAX.',
		template: 'splash',
		pagefind: false,
	}}
	hasSidebar={false}
>
	<div class="page home not-content">
		<Hero />

		<Section id="neuron" label="Neurons" role="membrane" title="A neuron keeps a charge, and spikes when it is full">
			<p>
				A spiking neuron adds its input to a membrane potential that leaks away over time. When the membrane reaches a threshold, the
				neuron sends a spike, a single 1, and resets. The rest of the time it sends nothing.
			</p>
			<p>
				Every sparx neuron is a small JAX dataclass with a <code>step</code>, and <code>sparx.run</code> scans one over time.
				The figure is that step, in your browser.
			</p>
			<CodeBlock fold code={neuron} colab={colab('neuron')} source={source('src/sparx/dynamics/ml.py')} />
			<a class="more" href="/learn/neuron/">Neurons, from LIF to Izhikevich</a>
			<LifScope slot="figure" />
		</Section>

		<Section id="train" label="Training" role="learn" title="Layers that train like any Flax module" flip>
			<p>
				A spike is a step function, so its derivative is zero almost everywhere and gradients cannot pass it. sparx keeps the spike exact
				on the way forward and uses a smooth surrogate's slope on the way back. Its layers are Flax modules over time-major arrays,{' '}
				<code>[T, B, ...]</code>, so <code>jit</code>, <code>grad</code>, <code>vmap</code>, optax and sharding work as they do for any
				network.
			</p>
			<CodeBlock fold code={train} colab={colab('train')} source={source('README.md')} />
			<a class="more" href="/learn/surrogate-gradients/">Teach a neuron when to fire</a>
			<SurrogatePlot slot="figure" />
		</Section>

		<Section id="pilot" label="The drone" role="spike" title="How the pilot learned to fly">
			<p>
				The network flying the drone at the top of this page is three sparx layers: 7 readings in, 64 and 64 LIF neurons, and two leaky
				integrators whose membranes set the rotors' thrust. Nothing showed it how to fly. Each training step flew {trained.batch} drones
				for {trained.horizon / 100} s through a model of their physics in JAX, and took the gradient of a cost led by their distance to their targets,
				through the spikes and through the physics.
			</p>
			<p>
				After {trained.steps.toLocaleString('en-US')} steps it brings the drone within 15 cm of a fixed target, and keeps it there,
				on {percent(evaluation.arrived)} of 1,000 random starts, and {percent(evaluation.arrived_from_inverted)} of those that began
				upside down, in a median of {evaluation.median_time_s.toFixed(2)} s.
			</p>
			<CodeBlock fold code={pilot} source={source('site/lab/pilot.py')} />
			<a class="more" href="/learn/drone/">Training, lesions and the check against sparx</a>
			<figure slot="figure" class="numbers">
				<div><strong>{percent(evaluation.arrived)}</strong><span>of 1,000 flights reach the target and stay</span></div>
				<div><strong>{percent(evaluation.arrived_thrown)}</strong><span>of 1,000 thrown and spun at random, about 4 m/s and 15 rad/s</span></div>
				<div><strong>{evaluation.median_time_s.toFixed(2)} s</strong><span>median time to arrive</span></div>
				<div><strong>{(evaluation.final_distance_median_m * 100).toFixed(1)} cm</strong><span>median distance after 6 s</span></div>
			</figure>
		</Section>

		<Section id="circuits" label="Circuits" role="bio" title="Circuits in millivolts and milliseconds" flip>
			<p>
				The same neuron protocol runs biological models in physical units, wired into populations and projections with delays, and
				simulated on one clock in NEST's order. Brunel's balanced network shifts between its regimes as inhibition and external drive
				change. The figure steps the network the code builds, in a worker in your browser.
			</p>
			<p>
				Current-based LIF, Izhikevich, STDP and the cortical microcircuit on one drawn network match NEST spike for spike. Conductance and
				adaptive models agree within stated margins. Chaotic networks, like this one, match in rate, irregularity and synchrony over seeds.
			</p>
			<CodeBlock fold code={brunel} colab={colab('networks')} source={source('src/sparx/graph/models.py')} />
			<a class="more" href="/learn/networks/">Brunel's regimes, and the whole fly brain</a>
			<BrunelRaster slot="figure" />
		</Section>

		<Section id="checked" label="Fidelity" role="bio" title="Every model is checked against a reference">
			<p>
				Each model is checked against what defines it: a float64 loop of its equations, the authors' code, or NEST and Brian2.
				The <a href="/docs/fidelity/">fidelity ledger</a> lists every check, its observed error and every known difference,
				and the <a href="/docs/status/">status</a> page what is not established.
			</p>
			<div slot="figure" class="checks" role="table" aria-label="Checks against references">
				<div class="row head" role="row">
					<span role="columnheader">Model</span><span role="columnheader">Reference</span><span role="columnheader">Result</span>
				</div>
				{
					checks.map((check) => (
						<div class="row" role="row">
							<span role="cell" class="model">{check.model}</span>
							<span role="cell" class="reference">{check.reference}</span>
							<span role="cell" class="result">
								<span class:list={['kind', check.kind]}>{kinds[check.kind as keyof typeof kinds]}</span>
								{check.result}
							</span>
						</div>
					))
				}
			</div>
		</Section>

		<Section id="results" label="Results" role="learn" title="Measured, with their conditions" flip>
			<p>
				These are short, untuned runs on a 4-core CPU, each beside its reference's number. No GPU or TPU numbers exist yet, and the
				full-length, multi-seed SHD comparison is still open.
			</p>
			<a class="more" href="/docs/guide/#results-in-detail">Commands, times and comparisons</a>
			<div slot="figure" class="results" role="table" aria-label="Results">
				{
					results.map((row) => (
						<div class="result-row" role="row">
							<span role="cell" class="task">{row.task}</span>
							<span role="cell" class="network">{row.network}</span>
							<span role="cell" class="accuracy">{row.accuracy}</span>
						</div>
					))
				}
			</div>
		</Section>

		<Explainers />

		<section class="closing">
			<h2>Install it</h2>
			<p>Python 3.12 or later, with JAX, Flax and dew. For a GPU or TPU, install the matching JAX first.</p>
			<Install />
			<p class="links">
				<a href="/docs/">Read the docs</a>
				<a href={repository}>GitHub</a>
				<a href="/docs/status/">What works, and what doesn't yet</a>
			</p>
		</section>
	</div>
</StarlightPage>

<style>
	.home {
		padding-inline: var(--sl-content-pad-x, 1rem);
	}
	.numbers {
		margin: 0;
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
		gap: 1px;
		background: var(--sx-line);
		border: 1px solid var(--sx-line);
		border-radius: 0.75rem;
		overflow: hidden;
	}
	.numbers div {
		background: var(--sx-panel);
		padding: 1.5rem 1.25rem;
		display: grid;
		gap: 0.5rem;
		align-content: start;
	}
	.numbers strong {
		font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 1.4rem + 1.4vw, 2.75rem);
		font-weight: 650;
		letter-spacing: -0.03em;
		color: var(--sx-ink);
		font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
		line-height: 1;
	}
	.numbers span {
		font-size: 0.875rem;
		line-height: 1.4;
		color: var(--sx-muted);
	}
	.checks,
	.results {
		border: 1px solid var(--sx-line);
		border-radius: 0.75rem;
		overflow: hidden;
		font-size: 0.8125rem;
		line-height: 1.45;
	}
	.row {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: auto 1fr;
		gap: 0.125rem 0.5rem;
		padding: 0.625rem 0.875rem;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--sx-line);
	}
	.row .result {
		grid-column: 1 / -1;
	}
	.row .reference::before {
		content: '· ';
	}
	.row.head {
		display: none;
	}
	.model {
		color: var(--sx-ink);
		font-weight: 550;
	}
	.reference {
		color: var(--sx-muted);
	}
	.result {
		color: var(--sx-ink-2);
	}
	.kind {
		display: inline-block;
		margin-right: 0.5rem;
		padding: 0 0.375rem;
		border-radius: 0.25rem;
		font-family: var(--sx-mono);
		font-size: 0.6875rem;
		line-height: 1.5rem;
		white-space: nowrap;
	}
	.kind.exact {
		color: var(--sx-bio);
		background: var(--sx-bio-soft);
	}
	.kind.tolerance {
		color: var(--sx-membrane);
		background: var(--sx-membrane-soft);
	}
	.kind.statistics {
		color: var(--sx-learn);
		background: var(--sx-learn-soft);
	}
	.row:first-of-type {
		border-top: 0;
	}
	@media (min-width: 40rem) {
		.row {
			grid-template-columns: 1.1fr 1fr 1.4fr;
			gap: 1rem;
			padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
		}
		.row .result {
			grid-column: auto;
		}
		.row .reference::before {
			content: none;
		}
		.row.head {
			display: grid;
			border-top: 0;
			font-size: 0.6875rem;
			font-family: var(--sx-mono);
			text-transform: uppercase;
			letter-spacing: 0.04em;
			color: var(--sx-muted);
			background: var(--sx-panel);
		}
	}
	.result-row {
		display: grid;
		gap: 0.25rem;
		padding: 0.875rem 1rem;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--sx-line);
	}
	.result-row:first-child {
		border-top: 0;
	}
	.task {
		color: var(--sx-ink);
		font-weight: 550;
	}
	.network {
		color: var(--sx-muted);
	}
	.accuracy {
		font-family: var(--sx-mono);
		font-size: 0.8125rem;
		color: var(--sx-ink);
	}
	.closing {
		max-width: 80rem;
		margin-inline: auto;
		padding-block: 5rem 6rem;
		display: grid;
		gap: 1rem;
		justify-items: start;
	}
	.closing h2 {
		margin: 0;
		font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 1.3rem + 1.6vw, 2.5rem);
		letter-spacing: -0.03em;
		font-weight: 650;
		color: var(--sx-ink);
	}
	.closing p {
		margin: 0;
		color: var(--sx-ink-2);
	}
	.closing .links {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 1.5rem;
		margin-top: 1rem;
	}
	.closing .links a {
		color: var(--sx-ink);
		font-weight: 550;
	}
</style>
